# EXPECT: which another imported module already binds
#
# Two modules with a top-level binding of the same name. The VM gives each its
# own env and both getters answer correctly; splicing merges them into one
# global. The shape this had before the guard is the worst a divergence can
# take: the module DICTS stayed correct (100 and 200, snapshots taken at
# different points) while the FUNCTIONS both read the merged global — so the
# obvious check passes and the actual behaviour is wrong.
import _mod_a
import _mod_b
print of (_mod_a.aget of null)
print of (_mod_b.bget of null)
